<title>CANADA: GM strike could deal Canadian economy serious blow.</title>
<headline>GM strike could deal Canadian economy serious blow.</headline>
<byline>Malina Poshtova Zang</byline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A prolonged strike at General Motors Corp's Canadian unit could seriously damage Canada's fledgling economic recovery, potentially shaving up to one percentage point off fourth-quarter growth, analysts said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;I think a short strike would have only a transitory effect, but a long one could be very damaging,&quot; said John McCallum, chief economist at the Royal Bank of Canada in Toronto.</p>
</text>
